(vector (map (:adr/consequences "{:shared_engine_different_layers \"net-babiniku and network-isekai both render VRM via the\\n                                    same kotoba-lang/kami-engine substrate, through\\n                                    different integration layers fit to each app's own\\n                                    stack/audience\", :sdk_validation \"validates kami-engine-sdk's webvr + pluggable-onScene design as reusable\\n                   across two unrelated domains (incident-response drills, AI-companion\\n                   roleplay)\", :new_backend_needed \"standalone backend (LLM chat + TTS + governor) and private data\\n                       store to build; nothing inherited automatically from\\n                       network-isekai's backend/\", :scaffold_shape_followup \"network-isekai-like scaffold (README + 90-docs/adr +\\n                            package.json, ADR-driven), not ai-gftd-isekai's dodaf\\n                            PROJECT.jsonld/OWNERS/nanoid shape -- net-babiniku is a\\n                            kami-engine app in network-isekai's lineage, not part of the\\n                            ai-gftd-*/ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp product-registry line\", :out_of_scope_followup \"exact LLM provider(s), pricing/currency model, and detailed\\n                          moderation policy are product decisions out of scope for this\\n                          architecture ADR\"}"), (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "gftdcojp/net-babiniku is a NEW, separate repo from gftdcojp/network-isekai -- both\n    render VRM avatars via the same kotoba-lang/kami-engine substrate, but through\n    different integration layers (Svelte + @etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk for net-babiniku vs\n    hand-rolled ClojureScript/reagent glue for network-isekai) and for different audiences\n    (private single-purpose AI-companion product vs open public forkable game platform)" "net-babiniku's product shape is modeled on isekaizero.ai (interactive AI stories,\n    choices-matter roleplay chat, per-character voice) but replaces its 2D visual-novel\n    character portraits with a live-rendered 3D VRM avatar (VTuber presentation), via\n    kami-engine-sdk's VrmViewer/createVrmEngine" "net-babiniku reuses kami-engine-sdk's `webvr` headless choice-scenario runner\n    (createIncidentVrEngine, langgraph/Pregel StateGraph, pluggable onScene renderer) --\n    originally built for cyber-drill's incident-response drills -- repurposed to\n    conversational roleplay content, supplying VrmViewer as the onScene renderer instead\n    of cyber-drill's vendor-private three.js scene" "AI-persona content is containment + governor per the existing Actors doctrine: the\n    LLM-persona node proposes {dialogue, emotion, motion-cue} only; a separate\n    ContentGovernor filters before anything renders to the VRM avatar or is spoken via\n    TTS; every commit/hold is appended to an audit ledger" "net-babiniku's data model is private/per-user (chat sessions, personas, avatar\n    customization), NOT network-isekai's public content-addressed everything-forkable EDN\n    model -- kotoba-style content-addressing may still be used internally for asset\n    caching only")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "net-babiniku-vrm-vtuber"), (:adr/related (vector "90-docs/adr/2607032400-network-isekai-primary-consolidation.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607041430-network-isekai-reagent-spa-consolidation.edn")), (:adr/status "proposed"), (:adr/id "adr-2607051800-net-babiniku-vrm-vtuber-design"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/amendments "[{:date \"2026-07-05\", :what \"frontend stack corrected to ClojureScript + reagent/re-frame + kami-webgpu +\\n          kotoba-lang/vrm, matching network-isekai's own toolchain exactly -- per direct\\n          user direction, superseding the :frontend and :turn_engine decisions above\\n          (Svelte 5 + @etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk + webvr's headless choice-scenario\\n          runner)\", :unchanged [\"the :ai_persona_containment decision (LLM-persona proposes only, a\\n                separate governor is the sole path to a renderable/speakable turn,\\n                append-only ledger) -- re-expressed in .cljc (babiniku.governor/\\n                review-turn) instead of TypeScript, gated by `nbb governor`\" \"the :data_model decision (private, per-user)\"], :retires [\"alternative #3 (reuse cyber-drill's three.js scene renderer) -- moot, no\\n              webvr/SDK dependency left to supply an onScene renderer for\"], :deployed \"Milestone 0 placeholder: a kami-webgpu render loop (placeholder box by\\n              default, real live VRM avatar via ?vrm=<url> through babiniku.vrm-bridge,\\n              adapted from isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc) + reagent/re-frame UI with a live\\n              governor demo, on Cloudflare Pages -- https://net-babiniku.pages.dev. No\\n              LLM backend, no TTS, no real chat yet.\"}]"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-05"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607051800: net-babiniku — a new gftdcojp product, AI VTuber/VRM companion chat, distinct from network-isekai but sharing the kami engine\n\n## Status\nProposed\n\n## Context\n\nUser direction (2026-07-05): design `gftdcojp/net-babiniku` as a **separate** repo from\n`gftdcojp/network-isekai`, using the **same kami engine**, shaped as a **VRM/VTuber-type**\napp in the spirit of [isekaizero.ai](https://www.isekaizero.ai/).\n\nResearch on isekaizero.ai (ISEKAI ZERO, ARX MEDIA SDN BHD, mobile app, #1 Games/#2\nEntertainment on the App Store as of May 2026): an **interactive AI story/roleplay** app —\nchat with LLM-driven characters, choices shape the narrative, an experimental \"Visual Novel\nMode\" adds background images + **character images with changing expressions/poses** + **per-\ncharacter TTS voice**. Backend is multi-LLM (Deepseek 3.2 default, switchable to\nGemini/Grok), dual-currency (free Mana / paid Arcane credits). Its character presentation is\n2D (visual-novel-style portraits with expression swaps), not a live 3D avatar.\n\n`network-isekai` (`90-docs/adr/2607032400-network-isekai-primary-consolidation.edn`,\n`90-docs/adr/2607041430-network-isekai-reagent-spa-consolidation.edn`) is the existing\nkami-engine web product: an **open, \"CodePen for games\"** platform — every game/dance-\nstage/asset is public, forkable, content-addressed EDN in Datomic via kotoba. It already has\na VRM feature (`:dance` stages — `kami.dance`/`kami-live` vocabulary, `isekai.stage.cljc` +\n`isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc` hand-rolled against `kami-web` wasm directly), but VRM avatars there\nare one mode among several (games/dance/assets/generate/studio), not the product's identity,\nand everything is public/forkable by design — wrong shape for private AI-companion chat\nsessions.\n\nSeparately, `kotoba-lang/kami-engine-sdk` (`@etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk`, Svelte 5,\nthree.js-free as of ADR-2605264300) already packages exactly the pieces a VTuber-style app\nneeds as a reusable SDK, built **after** network-isekai's own vrm-bridge glue was written:\n- `VrmViewer` + `createVrmEngine` — a live VRM avatar rendered end-to-end via the Rust+wgpu\n  WASM `KamiWasmExports` surface (no three.js, no DOM-side render loop to hand-write).\n- headless builders for **morph** (facial expression blend-shapes), **bone/motion** (pose/\n  gesture), **voice** (TTS), and **emotion** control.\n- `./webvr` — a **headless, choice-based scenario runner** (`createIncidentVrEngine`,\n  langgraph/Pregel StateGraph) with a pluggable `onScene` callback for rendering. Built for\n  cyber-drill's incident-response training drills (which supply their own three.js renderer\n  via `onScene`), but the shape — headless turn/state engine + swappable renderer — is\n  exactly what an isekaizero.ai-style \"choices matter\" branching conversation needs.\n\nNo existing gftdcojp product combines `webvr`'s choice engine with `VrmViewer` as the\n`onScene` renderer. `ai-gftd-isekai` (isekai.gftd.ai) was checked and is unrelated — a\nMinecraft-voxel-sandbox × creature-collection game sharing kami-engine's WebGPU renderer and\nthe \"isekai\" name only coincidentally.\n\n## Decision\n\nCreate **`gftdcojp/net-babiniku`**: a private, single-purpose product — chat with an\nLLM-driven character persona whose body is a **live-rendered 3D VRM avatar** (VTuber\npresentation) instead of isekaizero.ai's 2D visual-novel portraits, reusing `kami-engine`'s\nrender substrate via the SDK rather than reimplementing it.\n\n1. **Org/visibility:** `gftdcojp` (human-centric/business scope, per `repos.edn` `:orgs`),\n   **private** (per repos.edn `:orgs :visibility` policy for gftdcojp), plain-git child repo\n   registered in `manifest/repos.edn` `:extra-projects` → `manifest/west.yml`.\n\n2. **Frontend stack: Svelte 5 via `@etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk`, not network-isekai's\n   ClojureScript/reagent.** `VrmViewer`/`createVrmEngine` already is the live-avatar render\n   surface this product needs; network-isekai's `isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc`/`isekai.stage.cljc`\n   predate the SDK and hand-roll the same glue directly against `kami-web` wasm. No reason\n   for a second app to redo that work in CLJS when the SDK packages it for exactly this.\n\n3. **Turn engine: `kami-engine-sdk`'s `webvr` headless choice-scenario runner**\n   (`createIncidentVrEngine`, Pregel/langgraph StateGraph), repurposed from incident-response\n   drill content to conversational-roleplay content. net-babiniku is the SDK's **second**\n   `webvr` consumer (after cyber-drill) and its **first** `VrmViewer`-as-`onScene`-renderer\n   consumer (cyber-drill supplies its own vendor-private three.js scene) — validates the\n   headless-engine/pluggable-renderer split works across two unrelated domains.\n\n4. **Expression/motion mapping, data-driven like `kami.dance`'s pose-from-EDN:** each LLM\n   turn emits `{dialogue, emotion, motion-cue}`; `emotion` drives the SDK's morph builder\n   (facial blend-shape targets), `motion-cue` drives the bone/motion builder (idle/gesture\n   pose) — the same \"render state is a pure projection of data\" philosophy `kami.dance`\n   already uses for beat-synced dance poses, applied to conversation turns instead of a beat\n   grid.\n\n5. **Voice: the SDK's voice builder** drives per-character TTS, matching isekaizero.ai's\n   per-character-voice Visual Novel Mode but spoken through a live avatar instead of a static\n   portrait. net-babiniku stands up its **own** backend (LLM chat completion + TTS) —\n   independent deploy from network-isekai's `backend/` (Modal GPU: TRELLIS/image/TTS/music),\n   not a runtime dependency on it. Where the same *pattern* (Modal-GPU TTS service shape)\n   applies, copy-adapt rather than depend cross-repo — the same \"duplicate a small amount of\n   glue rather than couple two independent apps\" tradeoff `isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc`'s own\n   doc-comment already made explicit for character-creator's gpu-adapter.\n\n6. **AI-persona containment + governor, per the existing Actors doctrine (CLAUDE.md\n   Actors section; precedent: `isekai.moderation.cljc`).** The LLM-persona node proposes a\n   turn `{dialogue, emotion, motion-cue}` only; a separate `ContentGovernor` checks/filters\n   it before anything is ever rendered to the VRM avatar or spoken via TTS. Every\n   commit/hold is appended to an audit ledger. Non-negotiable for an AI-companion product —\n   this class of app is a known moderation surface, and \"babiniku\" (バ美肉,\n   embodying a VRM/VTuber persona) framing makes an explicit content gate more important, not\n   less.\n\n7. **Data model: private, not public/forkable.** Chat sessions, character personas, and\n   per-user avatar customization are private product data (per-user store), unlike\n   network-isekai's public content-addressed \"everything is forkable\" EDN model.\n   Kotoba-style content-addressing may still be used internally for asset caching (e.g.\n   avatar/voice asset dedup), but there is no public asset hub, no fork-by-URL UX.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- net-babiniku and network-isekai both render VRM avatars via the same underlying\n  `kotoba-lang/kami-engine` (kami-web wasm / kami-webgpu, Rust+wgpu), satisfying \"same kami\n  engine\" — but through different integration layers (SDK/Svelte vs hand-rolled CLJS glue),\n  each fit to its own app's stack and audience.\n- Validates `kami-engine-sdk`'s `webvr` + pluggable-`onScene` design as genuinely reusable\n  across two unrelated domains (incident-response drills, AI-companion roleplay) — a design\n  smell would be if only one consumer shape ever worked.\n- New standalone backend (LLM chat + TTS + governor) and its own private data store to\n  build; nothing here is inherited automatically from network-isekai's `backend/`.\n- Follow-up: scaffold shape is network-isekai-like (README + `90-docs/adr` + package.json,\n  ADR-driven), not `ai-gftd-isekai`'s dodaf `PROJECT.jsonld`/`OWNERS`/nanoid shape — net-\n  babiniku is a kami-engine app in the same lineage as network-isekai, not part of the\n  `ai-gftd-*`/`ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp` product-registry line.\n- Follow-up: exact LLM provider(s), pricing/currency model (if any), and moderation policy\n  detail are product decisions out of scope for this architecture ADR.\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n1. **Build it as a new mode/page inside `network-isekai`** (like `assets.html`/\n   `generate.html` today). Rejected — different audience (private product vs open platform)\n   and different data model (private chat sessions vs network-isekai's public forkable EDN);\n   forcing \"everything is public and forkable\" onto private AI-companion conversations is\n   architecturally wrong, not just a styling difference. Also would keep the ClojureScript/\n   re-frame stack instead of the SDK's native Svelte packaging.\n2. **Reimplement VRM rendering glue directly** (network-isekai's own\n   `isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc` + `isekai.stage.cljc` pattern) instead of depending on\n   `kami-engine-sdk`. Rejected — the SDK already packages `VrmViewer` + morph/bone/voice/\n   emotion builders for exactly this; redoing it in CLJS+JS glue duplicates real, already-\n   built work for no benefit.\n3. **Reuse cyber-drill's three.js scene renderer** as the `webvr` `onScene` implementation.\n   Rejected — cyber-drill's renderer is vendor-private and three.js-based; the SDK is\n   explicitly three.js-free (ADR-2605264300) and `VrmViewer`'s native wgpu path is the\n   better-fit, on-brand renderer for a VTuber avatar body.\n\n## References\n\n- `90-docs/adr/2607032400-network-isekai-primary-consolidation.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2607041430-network-isekai-reagent-spa-consolidation.edn`\n- `gftdcojp/network-isekai`: `src/isekai/vrm_bridge.cljc`, `src/isekai/stage.cljc`,\n  `src/isekai/moderation.cljc`, `README.edn` (\"Not only games — VRM dance stages too\")\n- `kotoba-lang/kami-engine-sdk` (`com-junkawasaki/kami-engine-sdk` checkout): `README.edn`\n  (`VrmViewer`/`createVrmEngine`, `./webvr` `createIncidentVrEngine`, three.js-free\n  ADR-0031/ADR-2605264300)\n- isekaizero.ai research (2026-07-05 web search): interactive AI stories, choices-matter\n  roleplay, Visual Novel Mode (2D character images + expression/pose swaps + per-character\n  TTS), multi-LLM backend, Mana/Arcane dual currency\n- `gftdcojp/ai-gftd-isekai` — checked, unrelated (voxel-sandbox game, name coincidence only)\n- CLAUDE.md \"Actors\" section — containment + independent governor + append-only ledger\n  doctrine, applied here to the LLM-persona/ContentGovernor split\n\n\n## Amendment (2026-07-05): frontend stack corrected to ClojureScript + reagent/re-frame\n\nPer direct user direction, decision #2 (Svelte 5 + `@etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk`) and\ndecision #3 (`webvr`'s headless choice-scenario runner as the turn engine) are **superseded**\nby: **ClojureScript + reagent/re-frame + `kami-webgpu` + `kotoba-lang/vrm`, matching\n`network-isekai`'s own toolchain exactly** (same `deps.edn` library coordinates —\n`kotoba-lang/kami-webgpu`, `kotoba-lang/vrm`, `re-frame/re-frame`, `reagent/reagent` — same\n`:local/root` relative paths, since both repos sit at `orgs/<org>/<repo>` depth).\n\n`net-babiniku/src/babiniku/vrm-bridge.cljc` is a direct adaptation of network-isekai's\n`isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc` (duplicated, not depended-on — the file's own precedent already\ncovers exactly this tradeoff). The render loop (`babiniku.web`) uses `kami.webgpu`'s\nrender-IR EDN directly (`kami.webgpu/draw!`, `kami.webgpu.mesh/draw!`) instead of the SDK's\n`VrmViewer` component — no Svelte, no `webvr` Pregel/StateGraph turn engine in this repo.\n\nThe containment-boundary decision (#6: LLM-persona proposes only, a separate governor is the\nsole path to a renderable/speakable turn, append-only ledger) is **unchanged** — re-expressed\nin `.cljc` (`babiniku.governor/review-turn`) instead of TypeScript, gated by `nbb governor`\n(matching network-isekai's `isekai.moderation.cljc` + `nbb moderation` convention). The\nprivate-data-model decision (#7) is also unchanged.\n\nDeployed (Milestone 0, placeholder): a kami-webgpu render loop (a placeholder box by\ndefault, a real live VRM avatar via `?vrm=<url>` through the adapted vrm-bridge) plus a\nreagent/re-frame UI with a live governor demo, on Cloudflare Pages —\nhttps://net-babiniku.pages.dev. No LLM backend, no TTS, no real chat yet.\n\nThis also **retires alternative #3** (\"reuse cyber-drill's three.js scene renderer\") as\nmoot — there is no `webvr`/SDK dependency left to supply an `onScene` renderer for."), (:adr/decision "{:repo {:org \"gftdcojp\", :visibility :private, :rationale \"human-centric/business scope per repos.edn :orgs; gftdcojp default\\n                     visibility is private per repos.edn :orgs :visibility (ADR-2607021330)\", :registration \"plain-git child repo, manifest/repos.edn :extra-projects ->\\n                        manifest/west.yml, --entry net-babiniku minimal-diff generation\"}, :frontend {:stack \"Svelte 5 via @etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk (VrmViewer/createVrmEngine), NOT\\n           network-isekai's ClojureScript/reagent\", :rationale \"the SDK already packages the live-avatar render surface (wgpu/WASM,\\n               three.js-free); network-isekai's isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc/isekai.stage.cljc\\n               predate the SDK and hand-roll the same glue directly against kami-web wasm\\n               -- no reason to redo that work in CLJS for a second app\"}, :turn_engine {:what \"kami-engine-sdk's `webvr` headless choice-scenario runner\\n          (createIncidentVrEngine, langgraph/Pregel StateGraph), repurposed from\\n          incident-response drill content to conversational-roleplay content\", :renderer \"VrmViewer supplied as the onScene callback -- net-babiniku is webvr's\\n              SECOND consumer (after cyber-drill) and FIRST VrmViewer-as-onScene consumer,\\n              validating the headless-engine/pluggable-renderer split across two\\n              unrelated domains\"}, :expression_motion {:model \"each LLM turn emits {dialogue emotion motion-cue}; emotion drives the SDK's\\n           morph builder (facial blend-shape targets), motion-cue drives the bone/motion\\n           builder (idle/gesture pose) -- data-driven render state, same philosophy as\\n           kami.dance's pose-from-EDN but keyed to conversation turns instead of a beat\\n           grid\"}, :voice {:what \"SDK's voice builder drives per-character TTS, matching isekaizero.ai's\\n          per-character-voice Visual Novel Mode but spoken through a live avatar\", :backend \"net-babiniku stands up its OWN backend (LLM chat completion + TTS) --\\n             independent deploy from network-isekai's backend/ (Modal GPU: TRELLIS/\\n             image/TTS/music); where the same Modal-GPU-TTS pattern applies, copy-adapt\\n             rather than cross-repo depend, matching isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc's own\\n             precedent for character-creator's gpu-adapter\"}, :ai_persona_containment {:pattern \"Actors doctrine (CLAUDE.md Actors section; precedent isekai.moderation.cljc):\\n             LLM-persona node proposes {dialogue emotion motion-cue} only; a separate\\n             ContentGovernor filters before anything renders to the VRM avatar or is\\n             spoken via TTS; every commit/hold appended to an audit ledger\", :non_negotiable true}, :data_model {:what \"private, per-user chat sessions / personas / avatar customization -- NOT\\n          network-isekai's public content-addressed everything-forkable EDN model\", :kotoba_use \"content-addressing may still be used internally for asset caching\\n                (avatar/voice asset dedup) only -- no public asset hub, no fork-by-URL\"}}"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/problem "{:source \"user direction 2026-07-05: design gftdcojp/net-babiniku, separate from\\n           gftdcojp/network-isekai, sharing the same kami engine, shaped as a VRM/VTuber\\n           app in the spirit of isekaizero.ai\", :investigated [\"isekaizero.ai (ISEKAI ZERO, ARX MEDIA SDN BHD): interactive AI story/roleplay mobile\\n    app, #1 Games/#2 Entertainment App Store (2026-05), chat with LLM characters +\\n    choices-matter narrative + experimental Visual Novel Mode (2D background/character\\n    images with expression/pose swaps + per-character TTS), multi-LLM backend\\n    (Deepseek 3.2 default, switchable Gemini/Grok), Mana(free)/Arcane(paid) dual currency\" \"network-isekai is an open 'CodePen for games' platform: games + VRM :dance stages\\n    (kami.dance/kami-live vocabulary, isekai.stage.cljc + isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc hand-rolled\\n    against kami-web wasm directly) + asset hub, everything public/forkable EDN in Datomic\\n    via kotoba -- VRM is one mode among several, not the product's identity, and the\\n    public/forkable data model is wrong for private AI-companion chat sessions\" \"kotoba-lang/kami-engine-sdk (@etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk, Svelte 5, three.js-free per\\n    ADR-2605264300) already packages VrmViewer/createVrmEngine (live VRM avatar via\\n    Rust+wgpu WASM KamiWasmExports, no three.js) + headless morph/bone/motion/voice/\\n    emotion builders + `./webvr` (createIncidentVrEngine, langgraph/Pregel StateGraph,\\n    pluggable onScene renderer) -- built after network-isekai's own vrm-bridge glue, for\\n    exactly this kind of app\" \"no existing product combines webvr's choice engine with VrmViewer as the onScene\\n    renderer; cyber-drill (the only current webvr consumer) supplies its own vendor-private\\n    three.js renderer for incident-response drills, an unrelated domain\" \"gftdcojp/ai-gftd-isekai checked and is unrelated -- a Minecraft-voxel-sandbox x\\n    creature-collection game (isekai.gftd.ai) sharing kami-engine's WebGPU renderer and the\\n    'isekai' name only coincidentally\"], :risk \"AI-companion/roleplay chat is a known content-moderation surface; 'babiniku'\\n         (バ美肉, embodying a VRM/VTuber persona) framing raises the stakes of getting the\\n         containment/governor boundary right from the start, not as a retrofit.\"}"), (:adr/alternatives "[{:option \"build it as a new mode/page inside network-isekai (like assets.html/\\n            generate.html today)\", :rejected_because \"different audience (private product vs open platform) and different\\n                       data model (private chat sessions vs public forkable EDN) --\\n                       architecturally wrong, not a styling difference; would also keep\\n                       the ClojureScript/re-frame stack instead of the SDK's native Svelte\\n                       packaging\"} {:option \"reimplement VRM rendering glue directly (network-isekai's own\\n            isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc + isekai.stage.cljc pattern) instead of depending on\\n            kami-engine-sdk\", :rejected_because \"the SDK already packages VrmViewer + morph/bone/voice/emotion\\n                       builders for exactly this; redoing it in CLJS+JS glue duplicates\\n                       real, already-built work for no benefit\"} {:option \"reuse cyber-drill's three.js scene renderer as the webvr onScene\\n            implementation\", :rejected_because \"cyber-drill's renderer is vendor-private and three.js-based; the SDK\\n                       is explicitly three.js-free (ADR-2605264300) and VrmViewer's native\\n                       wgpu path is the better-fit, on-brand renderer for a VTuber avatar\\n                       body\"}]"), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607051800: net-babiniku -- a new gftdcojp product, AI VTuber/VRM companion\n          chat, distinct from network-isekai but sharing the kami engine"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))